c Spec 104 T022 caps-fallback probe fixture — hand-constructed, minimal.
c Provenance: written for this probe (not reduced from a corpus keyboard).
c The [CAPS ...] / [NCAPS ...] rule forms mirror corpus usage in
c release/sil/sil_cameroon_azerty (its slash rules, CAPS/NCAPS pairs).
c
c Roles:
c   K_Q — the PROBE key. No rule names K_Q in any state, so a tap can
c         only produce via the KeymanWeb base-key fallback. Tapped on
c         default (control: fallback fires, 'q'), shift (control: 'Q')
c         and caps (the unsettled state).
c   K_B — the STATE WITNESS. Its caps-gated rule can fire only when the
c         tap genuinely presents the CAPITAL Lstate; its ncaps rule
c         fires otherwise. If the witness reads "caps" on the caps
c         layer, caps state demonstrably engaged — a silent caps K_Q
c         then means "no fallback in caps", never "caps never engaged".
c   K_C — secondary observation: a bare (state-free) rule, tapped on
c         the caps layer to record whether state-free bindings fire
c         under CAPITAL.

store(&VERSION) '10.0'
store(&NAME) 'Caps Probe'
store(&LAYOUTFILE) 'caps_probe.keyman-touch-layout'
store(&TARGETS) 'any'

begin Unicode > use(main)

group(main) using keys

+ [CAPS K_B] > 'caps-witness'
+ [NCAPS K_B] > 'ncaps-witness'
+ [K_C] > 'bare-rule'
